in, reigning from 1897 to 1918, and from February 1918 also regent of Mecklenburg-Strelitz.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-henry-prince-of-orange"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-henry-prince-of-orange.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick Henry, Prince of Orange</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick Henry, Prince of Orange, was stadtholder of most provinces of the Dutch Republic from 1625 to 1647.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-of-denmark"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-i-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick I of Denmark</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick I was king of Denmark from 1523 and of Norway from 1524 until 1533, a younger son of Christian I and duke of Schleswig-Holstein.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-of-prussia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-i-of-prussia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick I of Prussia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick I of Prussia succeeded as Elector Frederick III of Brandenburg in 1688.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-of-wurttemberg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-i-of-wurttemberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick I of Württemberg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick I was the last duke and first king of Württemberg.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-burgrave-of-nuremberg"><span class="enc-name">Frederick I, Burgrave of Nuremberg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick I was a count of Zollern, as Frederick III, who became burgrave of Nuremberg around 1192 through his marriage to Sophia of Raabs, heiress of the previous…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-duke-of-anhalt"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-i-duke-of-anhalt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick I, Duke of Anhalt</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick I succeeded his father Leopold IV Frederick as duke of Anhalt in 1871 and reigned until his death.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-duke-of-wurttemberg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-i-duke-of-wurttemberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick I, Duke of Württemberg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick I, Duke of Württemberg, ruled the County of Montbéliard from 1581 and inherited the Duchy of Württemberg in 1593.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-elector-of-brandenburg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-i-elector-of-brandenburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick I, Elector of Brandenburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick I, Elector of Brandenburg, was a Hohenzollern burgrave of Nuremberg who supported Sigismund's election as king.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-elector-of-saxony"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-i-elector-of-saxony.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick I, Elector of Saxony</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick I, called the Warlike, was a Wettin margrave of Meissen who became the first Wettin Elector of Saxony.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-elector-palatine"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-i-elector-palatine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick I, Elector Palatine</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick I, Elector Palatine, called the Victorious, governed the Palatinate from 1451 as guardian of his nephew and then as elector in his own right.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-grand-duke-of-baden"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-i-grand-duke-of-baden.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick I, Grand Duke of Baden</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick I ruled Baden as regent from 1852 and as grand duke from 1856 until his death.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-landgrave-of-hesse-homburg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-i-landgrave-of-hesse-homburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick I, Landgrave of Hesse-Homburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick I was the youngest son of Landgrave George I of Hesse-Darmstadt.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii"><span class="enc-name">Frederick II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick II was Holy Roman Emperor and King of Sicily in the thirteenth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-of-denmark"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-ii-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick II of Denmark</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick II was king of Denmark and Norway from 1559.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-of-legnica"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-ii-of-legnica.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick II of Legnica</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick II of Legnica was a Silesian Piast duke who ruled Legnica and from 1521 also Brzeg.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-elector-of-brandenburg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-ii-elector-of-brandenburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick II, Elector of Brandenburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick II, called Irontooth, was Elector of Brandenburg from 1440 to 1470, son of Frederick I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-grand-duke-of-baden"><span class="enc-name">Frederick II, Grand Duke of Baden</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick II was the last Grand Duke of Baden, reigning from 1907 to 1918, the son of Frederick I and a grandson of Emperor William I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-of-denmark"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-iii-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick III of Denmark</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick III was king of Denmark and Norway from 1648 to 1670.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-of-nuremberg"><span class="enc-name">Frederick III of Nuremberg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick III of Nuremberg was a Hohenzollern burgrave of Nuremberg who helped secure the election of Rudolf of Habsburg as King of the Romans in 1273.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-of-wied"><span class="enc-name">Frederick III of Wied</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick III of Wied was a German count who founded the town of Neuwied on the Rhine in 1653, near a village ruined in the Thirty Years' War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-duke-of-holstein-gottorp"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-iii-duke-of-holstein-gottorp.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick III, Duke of Holstein-Gottorp</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick III, Duke of Holstein-Gottorp, ruled from 1616 to 1659 and kept a cultured Lutheran court at Gottorp.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-elector-of-saxony"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-iii-elector-of-saxony.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick III, Elector of Saxony</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick III, Elector of Saxony, known as Frederick the Wise, ruled the Ernestine electorate from 1486 to 1525.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-elector-palatine"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-iii-elector-palatine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick III, Elector Palatine</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick III, Elector Palatine, called the Pious, came from the Palatinate-Simmern line and became elector in 1559.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-holy-roman-emperor"><span class="enc-name">Frederick III, Holy Roman Emperor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick III was a Habsburg duke of Inner Austria who became King of the Romans in 1440 and the last emperor crowned in Rome, in 1452.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-prince-of-salm-kyrburg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-iii-prince-of-salm-kyrburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick III, Prince of Salm-Kyrburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick III, Prince of Salm-Kyrburg, was a German prince who lived mainly in Paris, where he built the Hôtel de Salm, now the Palace of the Legion of Honour.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iv-duke-of-austria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-iv-duke-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick IV, Duke of Austria</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick IV, Duke of Austria, of the Habsburg dynasty, ruled Tyrol and the Habsburg lands in Further Austria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iv-duke-of-saxe-gotha-altenburg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-iv-duke-of-saxe-gotha-altenburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick IV, Duke of Saxe-Gotha-Altenburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick IV, Duke of Saxe-Gotha-Altenburg, was the last ruler of his line, succeeding his brother Augustus in 1822.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iv-prince-of-salm-kyrburg"><span class="enc-name">Frederick IV, Prince of Salm-Kyrburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick IV was the last reigning Prince of Salm-Kyrburg, a small German princely house of the Holy Roman Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-lugard"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-lugard.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick Lugard</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick Lugard was a British colonial administrator who became high commissioner of the Protectorate of Northern Nigeria in 1900.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-middleton"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-middleton.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick Middleton</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sir Frederick Middleton was a British army officer who commanded the Canadian militia from 1884 to 1890.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-moss"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-moss.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick Moss</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick Moss was a New Zealand politician who served as British Resident in the Cook Islands from 1891 to 1898.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-peake"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-peake.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick Peake</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick Peake, known as Peake Pasha, was a British army officer who founded and commanded the Arab Legion, the army of the Emirate of Transjordan, from the early…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-roberts-1st-earl-roberts"><span class="enc-name">Frederick Roberts, 1st Earl Roberts</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick Roberts, 1st Earl Roberts, was a British field marshal.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-seymour"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-seymour.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick Seymour</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick Seymour was a British colonial official who succeeded James Douglas as governor of the mainland Colony of British Columbia in 1864.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-stanley-arnot"><span class="enc-name">Frederick Stanley Arnot</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick Stanley Arnot (1858–1914) was a Scottish missionary of the Plymouth Brethren who travelled widely in south-central Africa.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-fair"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-the-fair.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick the Fair</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick the Fair was a Habsburg Duke of Austria and Styria from 1308 and German anti-king from 1314, elected by one faction against Louis IV of Bavaria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick the Great</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick the Great, Frederick II of Prussia, was king from 1740.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-v-of-the-palatinate"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederi