>Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick VII was the last Count of Toggenburg, ruling a large territory in eastern Switzerland that stretched from the Toggenburg valley to the Prättigau and Davos.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-constantine-prince-of-hohenzollern-hechingen"><span class="enc-name">Frederick William Constantine, Prince of Hohenzollern-Hechingen</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick William Constantine was the last Prince of Hohenzollern-Hechingen, reigning from 1838.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-i-of-prussia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-william-i-of-prussia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick William I of Prussia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick William I was King in Prussia from 1713 to 1740, known as the Soldier King.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-i-duke-of-saxe-weimar"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-william-i-duke-of-saxe-weimar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick William I, Duke of Saxe-Weimar</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick William I was a Saxon duke of the Ernestine line who received the lands around Weimar in the Erfurt Division of 1572.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-ii-of-prussia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-william-ii-of-prussia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Frederick William II of Prussia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Frederick William II was King of Prussia from 1786 to 1797, nephew and successor of Frederick the Great.</span></a>