="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">French Community</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The French Community was an association created by de Gaulle's constitution of 1958 to replace the French Union, offering colonies autonomy within a French framework.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/french-conquest-of-algeria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/french-conquest-of-algeria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">French conquest of Algeria</span><span class="enc-type">War · 1830–1903</span><span class="enc-snip">The French conquest of Algeria began with the capture of Algiers from its Ottoman-era regency in 1830 and continued for decades.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/french-conquest-of-bornu"><span class="enc-name">French conquest of Bornu</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 1900</span><span class="enc-snip">The French conquest of Bornu in 1900 followed the defeat and death of the warlord Rabih az-Zubayr, who had seized Bornu in 1893.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/french-conquest-of-corsica"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/french-conquest-of-corsica.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">French conquest of Corsica</span><span class="enc-type">War · 1768–1769</span><span class="enc-snip">The French conquest of Corsica followed the Treaty of Versailles of 1768, by which Genoa ceded its rights over the island to France.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/french-directory"><span class="enc-name">French Directory</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The French Directory was the five-member executive that governed the French First Republic from November 1795 to November 1799 under the Constitution of the Year III.</span></a></li><li class=